DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The wwccssttoommbbss() function converts a wide character string _w_c_s_t_r_i_n_g into a
     multibyte character string, _m_b_s_t_r_i_n_g, beginning in the initial conversion
     state.  Up to _n_b_y_t_e_s bytes are stored in _m_b_s_t_r_i_n_g.  Partial multibyte
     characters at the end of the string are not stored.  The multibyte char‐
     acter string is null terminated if there is room.

